ecutive squares","methodDirectNodeIds":{"consecutive-square-differences":["math:telescoping"]},"nodeIds":["math:telescoping","cnm_148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, y=5","reason":"The product is (log 3/log 2)(log 4/log 3)...(log 32/log 31)=log 32/log 2=log_2 32=5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1977_AMC_12_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h043"],"id":"change-base-and-cancel","label":"Change to a common base","methodDirectNodeIds":{"change-base-and-cancel":["cnm_h045","math:telescoping"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h045","math:telescoping","cnm_h043"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E. 179","reason":"Appending a list's mean does not change its mean, so a_3 through a_9 all equal (a_1 + a_2)/2. Thus (19 + a_2)/2 = 99, giving a_2 = 179.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1999_AMC_12_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"partial-sum-telescoping","label":"Telescope the partial sums","methodDirectNodeIds":{"partial-sum-telescoping":["math:telescoping"]},"nodeIds":["math:telescoping"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 7/2","reason":"For j=1,...,124, x_j=log(j+4)/log(j+3). Their product telescopes to log(128)/log(4)=7/2. Equivalently, if P is the product, then 4^P=128.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["Retaining the logarithmic route does not mean logarithms or explicit telescoping are universally required; the power-chaining alternative remains mathematically valid."],"questionId":"2005_AMC_12B_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"id":"telescoping-logarithms","label":"Change base and cancel","nodeIds":["cnm_h043","cnm_h045","math:telescoping"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cn