et a=log_2 5. Then 2<a<3 and floor(867a)=2013. For n=0,...,866, the number of eligible m in the nth gap is floor((n+1)a)-floor(na)-2; these m all lie in the required range. Summing telescopes to 2013-2·867=279.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2014_AMC_12A_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"telescope-floor-differences","label":"Sum floor differences","methodDirectNodeIds":{"telescope-floor-differences":["cnm_h043","math:floor-ceiling","math:telescoping"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h043","math:floor-ceiling","math:telescoping"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 11","reason":"Set L_n=log_7(a_n) and u_n=log_7(n). Then L_3=u_3/u_2 and L_n=(u_n/u_(n-1))L_(n-1), giving L_2019=u_2019/u_2=log_2(2019). Since 2^10.5<2019<2^11, this logarithm lies between 10.5 and 11 and rounds to 11.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_12A_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"telescope-logarithmic-ratios","label":"Telescope logarithmic ratios","methodDirectNodeIds":{"telescope-logarithmic-ratios":["cnm_h044","cnm_h045","cnm_h200","math:telescoping"]},"nodeIds":["math:telescoping","cnm_h044","cnm_h045","cnm_h200"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 658 square units","reason":"The individual surfaces total 6(1²+2²+...+7²)=6(140)=840. The six interfaces hide twice 1²+2²+...+6²=91, so the exposed area is 840-2(91)=658, including the bottom.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2020_AMC_10A_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"separate-vertical-and-horizontal-surfaces","label":"Count sides, tops, and bottom","methodDirectNodeIds":{"separate-vertical-and-horizontal-surfaces":["cnm